{
  "cdmVersionRange": ">=5.0.0",
  "_README": "Antihypertensive exposure outside an inpatient stay: the medication half of the mFI-5 hypertension item (1 point). Subramaniam 2018 (from ACS NSQIP HYPERMED) scores hypertension only when it requires medication. REVISED 2026-11-06 to match the OHDSI Phenotype Library: the concept set is the drug-ingredient sets of PL 1046 (thiazide and thiazide-like diuretics: chlorthalidone, hydrochlorothiazide, indapamide, metolazone), PL 1047 (dihydropyridine calcium channel blockers: amlodipine, felodipine, isradipine, nicardipine, nifedipine, nisoldipine) and PL 1049 (beta blockers: 12 ingredients), each with descendants, plus ACE inhibitors and ARBs by ATC third level with descendants (C09A 21601783, C09B 21601801, C09C 21601822, C09D 21601832), because the library has no ACE-inhibitor or ARB cohort. The PL cohorts are new-user, first-exposure, nested-in-hypertension designs; only their drug concept sets are adopted here (deviation: any outpatient exposure in the window, not first exposure). Deliberately NOT included, as in the PL: loop and potassium-sparing diuretics, non-dihydropyridine CCBs, centrally acting agents, hydralazine and other C02 drugs, which have common non-hypertensive uses or are not first-line. The item also requires a hypertension diagnosis at any time before index (cohort 9100022, the same 316866 set as PL 1046/1047/1049), combined at score level via cohort_map.csv and_cohort_id, the insulin pattern (9100007 AND 9100021). Outpatient rule identical to 9100007: no inpatient visit (9201, 262, with descendants) spans the exposure start date; exposures with no visit link are kept. Window (set in cohort_map.csv, not here): 365 days before index, chosen over the NSQIP-literal 30 days because EHR medication lists are sparse. PrimaryCriteriaLimit / QualifiedLimit / ExpressionLimit are all All and EndStrategy is StartDate+0, like every covariate cohort here.",
